From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 07:47:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] quickjs: Bump servo-quickjs for three QuickJS-only memory
 leaks

servo-quickjs c38af5c brings three fixes for memory that QuickJS kept
and SpiderMonkey frees:
- Q41: the contents of an Rc shared by several DOM objects were never
  traced, so the cycle collector could not see through them. A
  CustomElementDefinition is shared by the registry and every element
  created from it, so a window that created one custom element was
  never freed: every same-site navigation and iframe of such a page
  stayed alive. Shared Rcs are now traced once per collector pass,
  when all their owners are reachable from the GC graph.
- Q42: FinalizationRegistry cleanup jobs went to QuickJS's own job
  list, which nothing runs while Servo's job queue is installed, and
  each held its realm forever. They are dropped instead: cleanup
  callbacks still never run, as with SpiderMonkey, where Servo sets no
  host cleanup callback.
- Q43: AddAssociatedMemory and RemoveAssociatedMemory have a GC
  trigger of their own, like SpiderMonkey's malloc threshold. Garbage
  canvases, whose bitmaps Servo reports that way, reached 10-27 GB and
  thousands of canvas threads before a collection.

The new Request(...).clone() subtest of
fetch-body-does-not-leak-document.https.html passes with QuickJS now.
WebGL framebuffer-to-texture.html tests #8 and #9 become intermittent
with QuickJS. Servo rejects the test's blits from a renderbuffer to a
texture with INVALID_OPERATION, since get_attachment_formats() knows
only renderbuffer formats (#6, #7 and #10 fail on every build), and
does not zero-initialize texStorage2D textures. So #8 and #9 read
whatever memory the GL driver hands to the texture: zeros on llvmpipe,
and on a GPU sometimes buffers that WebGL objects of earlier tests
freed when the garbage collector finalized them. The fixes change when
collections run: the tests failed in 1 of 11 parallel runs with the
old shim and in about half with the new one.

Validation: QuickJS release builds of aecb1d2a597 (this commit's parent before patches 128 and 129, which change only CI and docs) with servo-quickjs 2de9592 and with c38af5c's tree. 20 same-site navigations of a page with a custom element or a FinalizationRegistry: live realms 22 against 2, QuickJS heap 75 MiB against 4 MiB. 48 iframe page states, 20 frames each: 47 free every frame (listenerOnParent retains its frames by design, on both engines). 15 s of garbage 512x512 canvases without a forced GC: 10-27 GB against a 770 MiB peak, as on SpiderMonkey. Full WPT with --js-engine quickjs on both builds (58,638 tests), then the 29 tests that differed 3 more times on each, and builds with Q41 alone and Q41 and Q42 bisecting the WebGL tests: the only consistent difference is the Request clone subtest above (Q41 alone fixes it); the WebGL tests and two sanitizer-inert-document.html subtests are intermittent on both builds. The custom-elements, shadow-dom, streams, dom and FileAPI directories under QJS_VERIFY_TRACING=1: 1,837 tests as expected. GenUI, the three React apps, mossel and Wikipedia, 5 loads each: CPU and peak memory unchanged within noise. DOM churn of 30,000 custom elements per task pays +34% in batches that follow an explicit collection, which resets the new trigger, and nothing in the first batch. This commit's own build, from the git rev: both tests with changed expectations as expected 3 of 3 times, and the custom element and FinalizationRegistry navigation pages keep 2 realms.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent wrote the servo-quickjs changes, bumped the pin, updated the two expectations and ran the checks above)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml                         | 2 +-
 .../fetch-body-does-not-leak-document.https.html.ini      | 4 ----
 .../rendering/framebuffer-to-texture.html.ini             | 8 ++++++++
 3 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml b/support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml
index cb7fc2eb69f..d3808421ee8 100644
--- a/support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml
+++ b/support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml
@@ -5,4 +5,4 @@
 # were tested with. The shim's version must match the mozjs version that Cargo.toml requires, or
 # Cargo leaves the patch unused.
 [patch.crates-io]
-mozjs = { git = "https://github.com/openharmony-rs/servo-quickjs", rev = "2de95922804e5ec0876f3106097b46d0f62bd0c9" }
+mozjs = { git = "https://github.com/openharmony-rs/servo-quickjs", rev = "c38af5cbaf6ac252a65a81ff42b27b0097c19f7f" }
diff --git a/tests/wpt/mozilla/meta/memory/fetch-body-does-not-leak-document.https.html.ini b/tests/wpt/mozilla/meta/memory/fetch-body-does-not-leak-document.https.html.ini
index 5af81b3bfe5..67c5e048cbd 100644
--- a/tests/wpt/mozilla/meta/memory/fetch-body-does-not-leak-document.https.html.ini
+++ b/tests/wpt/mozilla/meta/memory/fetch-body-does-not-leak-document.https.html.ini
@@ -4,7 +4,3 @@
 
   ['<script>fetch("/common/slow.py?delay=60000", {method: "POST", duplex: "half", body: new ReadableStream({start(c) { c.enqueue(new Uint8Array([1\])); }})});</script>' does not leak the document]
     expected: FAIL
-
-  ['<script>new Request("/common/slow.py?delay=60000", {method: "POST", body: "data"}).clone();</script>' does not leak the document]
-    expected:
-      if js_engine == "quickjs": FAIL
diff --git a/tests/wpt/webgl/meta/conformance2/rendering/framebuffer-to-texture.html.ini b/tests/wpt/webgl/meta/conformance2/rendering/framebuffer-to-texture.html.ini
index c789b921fe3..5355f59e948 100644
--- a/tests/wpt/webgl/meta/conformance2/rendering/framebuffer-to-texture.html.ini
+++ b/tests/wpt/webgl/meta/conformance2/rendering/framebuffer-to-texture.html.ini
@@ -7,3 +7,11 @@
 
   [WebGL test #7]
     expected: FAIL
+
+  [WebGL test #8]
+    expected:
+      if js_engine == "quickjs": [PASS, FAIL]
+
+  [WebGL test #9]
+    expected:
+      if js_engine == "quickjs": [PASS, FAIL]
